    <h2>4. How to Balance Manifold Flow Meters Step-by-Step</h2>
    <p>
      Modern stainless steel radiant heating manifolds feature sight-glass flow meters on the supply header and micrometer balancing pin valves on the return header:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Turn Off Boiler Burner:</strong> Run the circulator pump on high speed with room thermostats calling for heat so all zone actuator heads are 100% open.</li>
      <li><strong>Open All Flow Meters:</strong> Twist the top red retaining rings counter-clockwise to unlock the flow meters, and back out all circuit valves fully.</li>
      <li><strong>Identify the Longest Loop (Index Run):</strong> The longest PEX loop (e.g., a 290-foot living room circuit) has the greatest friction. Leave this loop wide open.</li>
      <li><strong>Choke Down Shorter Loops:</strong> On shorter loops (e.g., a 120-foot powder room circuit), slowly twist the flow meter valve clockwise. Watch the red indicator disc sink until it reads exactly the engineered target GPM (e.g., 0.35 GPM).</li>
      <li><strong>Lock the Retaining Collar:</strong> Snap the red locking ring back into position to prevent thermal vibration from shifting the valve setting.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

